From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kylechar <kylechar@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 06:30:22 -0700
Subject: Fix ImageContext thread safety

SkiaOutputSurfaceImpl was resetting the ImageContextImpl SkImage in two
places. This isn't thread safe as it's possible SkImage is being
accessed on the GPU thread at the same time.

First, before sending the ImageContextImpl to the GPU main thread to be
deleted. This just wasn't needed.

Second, it was resetting non-overlay render pass SkImages each time they
were drawn. This was in case the render pass backing changed and a new
SkImage was needed. SkiaRenderer::UpdateRenderPassTextures() already
calls RemoveRenderPassResource() for any render pass backings that need
to be reallocated which deletes the ImageContextImpl. A new
ImageContextImpl and SkImage will be created in that case.

Bug: 574030524
Change-Id: Ic25d3d10daf8f719757a42d73710dbab7095328e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8608392
Commit-Queue: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Bo Liu <boliu@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1723735}

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
external_use_client.h on this branch predates the sync_tokens_ vector and
still carries paint_op_buffer_/clear_color_ accessors, so the header hunks
were applied by hand: SetImage() moved below the accessors with upstream's
comment, clear_image() moved to a new protected section, mailbox_ and
texture_target_ made const, and the two thread-safety comments updated. No
member was added or removed beyond the upstream diff; the single sync_token_
member is kept as-is. skia_output_surface_impl.cc merged without changes.

